      "evidence_type": "published tag insertion in the same loop or domain",
      "functional_impact_measured": "Surface expression detected by flow cytometry for tagged FL-CD19 variants; specific functional assays (e.g., signaling, CAR-T killing) NOT MEASURED for the tagged constructs in isolation.",
      "confidence": "medium",
      "rationale": "L3 (PMC6189457) reports that epitope tags were cloned into exon 1 of full-length, membrane-anchored CD19 for surface flow cytometry detection. Exon 1 of CD19 encodes the signal peptide (aa 1-19) and the beginning of the extracellular domain (~aa 20-61), placing any tag within this exon on the extracellular face. No specific residue number is given, so this remains a region-level site. The exon 1 ECD segment is entirely within the extracellular span (20-291) and far from the TM boundary. Full-length CD19 retroviral constructs bearing HA, FLAG, VSVg, and His epitope tags cloned into exon 1 of the intact membrane-anchored protein, used for flow cytometry surface detection of CD19 variants (including immunotherapy-resistant 105R and \u0394ex2). Exon 1 encodes the signal peptide and the N-terminal portion of the ECD (approximately aa 1-61); the tag was placed in exon 1 to avoid interference with exon 2 mutations.",
      "sources": [
        {
          "pmid": 30104252,
          "citation": "PMID 30104252",
          "claim": "The tags were cloned into exon 1 or 3 to avoid interference with exon 2 mutations."
        }
      ],
