  "literature_notes": "L4 and L5 (PMC8155657) describe yeast surface display of the CD19 ECD as an Aga2p-HA-(G4S)3-CD19-ECD-cmyc fusion construct. Although yeast surface display is membrane-anchored (via Aga2p-Aga1p), this is not a full-length native CD19 construct \u2014 it is the isolated ECD fused to a yeast display scaffold, not the intact membrane protein. These lines were therefore disqualified per the rule requiring a full-length membrane-anchored construct. L6 (PMC10754921) describes the same yeast surface display approach (Aga2p-HA-SF-CD19(Pro20-Pro278)-cmyc) and was similarly disqualified. L2 (PMC6189457) provides context for the same experimental system as L3 and was subsumed into the L3-grounded sites. The exon 1 and exon 3 sites from L2/L3 cannot be pinned to specific residues because the paper names only the exon, not the exact junction residue; they are reported as region-level sites with null insert_after_residue.",
